n provide a broad overview and observatio…\nUSER: Mixed methods could provide both quantitative data from surveys and qualitative insights from interviews, offering a comprehensive view. However, for my exploratory research question, the depth and nu…\nASSISTANT: Mary, you\'ve done a great job reflecting on the strengths and limitations of mixed methods. You\'re right that mixed methods can provide a comprehensive view by combining quantitative and qualitative d…\nUSER: I feel more confident in my decision to use semi-structured interviews because they align well with my exploratory research question and allow for deep, nuanced insights into teachers\' perceptions. Ot…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it\'s fantastic to see you feel more confident in your decision to use semi-structured interviews. You\'ve done an excellent job of reflecting on the alignment between your research question and t…\n\nSurvey:\nQ1: How well did the supervisor understand what you were confused or uncertain about? [1 (not at all) to 5 (completely)]\nQ2: Did the questions and guidance feel right for your level — not too directive, not too vague? [1 (very poorly calibrated) to 5 (perfectly calibrated)]\nQ3: Did you feel safe to express uncertainty or confusion without embarrassment? [1 (not at all) to 5 (completely)]\nQ4: How efficient was the conversation — did it take the right number of turns to reach clarity? [1 (very inefficient) to 5 (very efficient)]\nQ5: Overall, how satisfied are you with this supervisory interaction? [1 (very unsatisfied) to 5 (very satisfied)]\nQ_open: What was the most helpful thing the supervisor did, and what could have been better? [open text]<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.05, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=500, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, pr