ur PhD.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nMy research question is about how primary-school teachers perceive using digital tools for teaching geography. I was thinking of using semi-structured interviews with about 10 teachers. I haven't really considered other methods yet, so I'm not entirely sure if this is the best way to go.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nGreat, Mary! Your research question is clear and focused on understanding teachers' perceptions of digital tools in geography. You're considering semi-structured interviews with around 10 teachers, which is a thoughtful approach. Can you tell me a bit more about why you're leaning towards interviews? What do you think they might help you achieve that other methods might not?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nMy research question is about how primary-school teachers perceive using digital tools for teaching geography. I was thinking of using semi-structured interviews with about 10 teachers. I haven't really considered other methods yet, so I'm not entirely sure if this is the best way to go.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nYou've mentioned that you're considering semi-structured interviews with about 10 teachers. What are some reasons you think interviews might be a good fit for your research question? How do you think they might help you understand teachers' perceptions of digital tools in geography?<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nUNDERSTANDING_LEVEL: ", params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=0.7, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=350, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=None), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
